    days: [52],
    problems: [
      ["","Implement Min Heap","tuf-implement-min-heap","M",null,"https://takeuforward.org/practice/dsa/implement-min-heap?source=strivers-a2z-dsa-sheet","Implement a min-heap on an array: insert, getMin, extractMin, heapSize, isEmpty, changeKey(index, value).",[["ops = insert 4, insert 1, insert 10, getMin, heapSize, isEmpty, extractMin, changeKey 0 16, getMin","[null, null, null, 1, 3, false, null, null, 10]","After removing 1 the heap holds 4 and 10; changing 4 to 16 leaves 10 as the minimum."],["ops = insert 5, extractMin, isEmpty","[null, null, true]","After removing the only value the heap is empty."],["ops = insert 3, insert 3, insert 7, extractMin, getMin, heapSize","[null, null, null, null, 3, 2]","One 3 is removed; the other 3 is still the minimum and two values remain."]],["1 <= n <= 10^5","-10^5 <= nums[i] <= 10^5"],"Store the tree in an array: children of i are at 2i + 1 and 2i + 2. After a change, sift up or sift down to fix the order."],
      ["","Implement Max Heap","tuf-implement-max-heap","M",null,"https://takeuforward.org/practice/dsa/implement-max-heap?source=strivers-a2z-dsa-sheet","Implement a max-heap on an array: insert, getMax, extractMax, heapSize, isEmpty, changeKey(index, value).",[["ops = insert 4, insert 1, insert 10, getMax, heapSize, isEmpty, extractMax, changeKey 0 16, getMax","[null, null, null, 10, 3, false, null, null, 16]","After removing 10 the heap holds 4 and 1; changing 4 to 16 makes 16 the maximum."],["ops = insert 5, extractMax, isEmpty","[null, null, true]","After removing the only value the heap is empty."],["ops = insert 3, insert 3, insert 7, extractMax, getMax, heapSize","[null, null, null, null, 3, 2]","7 is removed; a 3 is the new maximum and two values remain."]],["1 <= n <= 10^5","-10^5 <= nums[i] <= 10^5"],"Same array layout as a min-heap, with the comparison flipped: a parent must be at least as large as its children."],
      ["","Heapify Algorithm","tuf-heapify-algorithm","M",null,"https://takeuforward.org/practice/dsa/heapify-algorithm?source=strivers-a2z-dsa-sheet","nums is a min-heap. Set nums[ind] = val, then sift it up or down to restore the heap. Return the array.",[["nums = [1, 4, 5, 5, 7, 6], ind = 5, val = 2","[1, 4, 2, 5, 7, 5]","2 is smaller than its parent 5, so they swap; 2 is not smaller than 1, so it stops."],["nums = [2, 3, 4, 8, 9], ind = 0, val = 10","[3, 8, 4, 10, 9]","10 sinks below 3, then below 8."],["nums = [1, 3, 2], ind = 1, val = 0","[0, 1, 2]","0 is smaller than its parent 1, so they swap."]],["1 <= nums.length <= 10^5","-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4","0 <= ind < nums.length","-10^4 <= val <= 10^4","nums represents a min-heap"],"Compare the new value with its parent. If it is smaller, move it up; otherwise compare it with its smaller child and move it down."],
      ["","Build heap from a given Array","tuf-build-heap-from-a-given-array","M",null,"https://takeuforward.org/practice/dsa/build-heap-from-a-given-array?source=strivers-a2z-dsa-sheet","Turn the array into a min-heap in place in O(n) (sift down from the last parent to the root). Any valid heap is accepted; the example shows the one bottom-up building gives.",[["nums = [6, 5, 2, 7, 1, 7]","[1, 5, 2, 7, 6, 7]","5 and 1 swap, then 6 sinks past 1 and 5."],["nums = [9, 8, 7, 6, 5]","[5, 6, 7, 9, 8]","9 and 8 sink below the smaller children."],["nums = [1, 2, 3]","[1, 2, 3]","Already a min-heap."]],["1 <= nums.length <= 10^5","-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4"],"Leaves are already heaps. Start at the last parent and sift each node down, moving toward the root."],
      ["","Check if an array represents a min heap","tuf-check-if-an-array-represents-a-min-heap-","M",null,"https://takeuforward.org/practice/dsa/check-if-an-array-represents-a-min-heap-?source=strivers-a2z-dsa-sheet","Return true if every parent is <= its children (array form: children of i are 2i+1 and 2i+2).",[["nums = [10, 20, 30, 21, 23]","true","10 ≤ 20, 30 and 20 ≤ 21, 23."],["nums = [10, 20, 30, 25, 15]","false","20 has the child 15, which is smaller."],["nums = [5, 5, 5]","true","Equal values are allowed."]],["1 <= nums.length <= 10^5","-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4","The array represents a complete binary tree."],"Only parents need checking. Which indices have at least one child?"],
      ["","Convert Min Heap to Max Heap","tuf-convert-min-heap-to-max-heap","M",null,"https://takeuforward.org/practice/dsa/convert-min-heap-to-max-heap?source=strivers-a2z-dsa-sheet","Rearrange a min-heap array into a max-heap. Any valid max-heap is accepted; the example shows the one bottom-up building gives.",[["nums = [10, 20, 30, 21, 23]","[30, 23, 10, 21, 20]","The largest value 30 rises to the root."],["nums = [1, 2, 3]","[3, 2, 1]","3 rises to the root."],["nums = [3, 5, 9, 6, 8, 20, 10, 12, 18, 9]","[20, 18, 10, 12, 9, 9, 3, 5, 6, 8]","Each parent ends up at least as large as its children."]],["1 <= nums.length <= 10^5","-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4","nums represents a min-heap"],"You can ignore the fact that it is a min-heap: build a max-heap from the array bottom-up."],
      ["","Heap Sort","tuf-heap-sort","H",null,"https://takeuforward.org/practice/dsa/heap-sort?source=strivers-a2z-dsa-sheet","Sort the array in place with heap sort: build a max-heap, then move the top to the end n - 1 times.",[["nums = [7, 4, 1, 5, 3]","[1, 3, 4, 5, 7]","The values in increasing order."],["nums = [5, 5, 1]","[1, 5, 5]","The duplicate 5s stay together."],["nums = [-2, 10, 0, 3]","[-2, 0, 3, 10]","Negative values sort first."]],["1 <= nums.length <= 10^5","-10^4 <= nums[i] <= 10^4","nums[i] may contain duplicate values."],"With a max-heap, the largest value is at index 0. Swap it to the end, shrink the heap, and fix the root."]
    ]
